  "legacyHoldReasons": {
    "f_juapfne3wzqtc": "DBIA171 (p.34) compares Tamil cūci/ūci, Malayalam sūci/tūśi, Kannada sūci/sūji/sūje, Telugu sūdi and other Dravidian needle forms with Sanskrit sūc-, Prakrit sui- and Hindi sui/sūji. The selected survey forms require source-local borrowing-route evidence, not automatic inherited links or a jump to Sanskrit. The current DBIA Indo-Aryan node is incorrectly headed cūcub (the Parji comparator in the OCR); it is not a usable donor.",
    "f_vzzarxibw45ye": "DBIA318(p.58) treats Kannada baṭṭe, Kodagu batte, Tulu baṭṭe, Telugu baṭṭa and Kota bat as loans ultimately from Sanskrit paṭṭa cloth, explicitly rejecting derivation from vastra. The selected survey forms need an immediate-donor/transmission analysis; do not label them inherited or automatically jump to Sanskrit. Compound/paired responses also require constituent analysis.",
    "f_2eay6hfaunv3s": "DEDR2629 compares Tamil cīrai/cīlai, Malayalam cīla/śīla, Kannada sīre and Gondi cīla/sīle, but explicitly discusses Sanskrit cīra versus cela and probable contamination. The survey matches do not settle inheritance, borrowing or the immediate donor; retain this caveat before assigning a historical relation.",
    "f_rc4isy4v7mzam": "DEDR2629 compares Tamil cīrai/cīlai, Malayalam cīla/śīla, Kannada sīre and Gondi cīla/sīle, but explicitly discusses Sanskrit cīra versus cela and probable contamination. The survey matches do not settle inheritance, borrowing or the immediate donor; retain this caveat before assigning a historical relation.",
    "f_p5khcuhfkynry": "The full DEDR appendix57 places Tamil/Malayalam vāl, Kannada bāla, Kota vālm, Kodagu bālï and Telugu vālamu alongside CDIAL11572 vāla-/vāra-. The existing appendix parent f_wqel4vcg76coc has an empty Form label. Do not attach these survey responses to an unnamed parent or skip to a remote Sanskrit ancestor before the historical route and immediate donor/parent are resolved.",
    "f_of7be3dyjfycq": "The full DEDR appendix57 places Tamil/Malayalam vāl, Kannada bāla, Kota vālm, Kodagu bālï and Telugu vālamu alongside CDIAL11572 vāla-/vāra-. The existing appendix parent f_wqel4vcg76coc has an empty Form label. Do not attach these survey responses to an unnamed parent or skip to a remote Sanskrit ancestor before the historical route and immediate donor/parent are resolved.",
    "f_hute2t6uuavug": "DEDR5496(a) explicitly gives veḷḷi star/Venus/silver and Kodagu boḷḷi mīnï morning star. These simple veḷḷi/beḷḷi or white/silver + star responses need that subsection, but the current parent is labelled veṇ-ṇey butter from subsection (b). Hold until the parent scope is repaired; do not attach a star or its white component to the butter head.",
    "f_v5h6ro3bimtlo": "Full DBIA233(a) gives Tamil pakkam, Malayalam pakkam/pakkal, Kannada pakka and Telugu pakka side/near, deriving the family from Sanskrit pakṣa- and Prakrit pakkha-. The survey form is a strong lexical match, but the immediate borrowing route for this particular language is not established; do not encode an inherited Dravidian reflex or silently choose Sanskrit over a regional intermediary.",
    "f_yixbomqwjidhc": "The survey garlic name begins veḷḷa-/veḷa-/beḷḷa- white, but current d5496 is veṇṇey butter, not the adjective needed for the compound. Retain for parent repair and separate second-component checking (veṅkāyam versus pūṇṭu). Do not encode a butter component or guess the whole compound from the garlic gloss."
  }
}
